+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+This project's cache eviction policy is LRU (Least Recently Used) combined with a 300-second time-to-live (TTL). Cache entries expire after 300 seconds regardless of access frequency, while LRU eviction removes the least-recently-accessed items once the cache reaches capacity, giving both age-based and access-based invalidation.
